 "description": "Owner request 2026-11-11 sections 2 and 3, device-independent\nportion.\n\nResolution from the real source (section 2):\n- nativePreviewOpen's first-frame dimensions are kept through the open\n  boundary: PreviewSession and PreviewRenderer carry width/height\n  (EditorPreviewSession gains them with a 0 default; encoded sessions\n  report their open info), and the clip info sheet prefers the\n  session-recorded size over the persisted import stat\n  (EditorPreviewLogic.recordedWidth). An old import that recorded 0x0\n  shows what is known — never a re-import demand.\n\nPause and clip end land on the source resolution (section 2):\n- PreviewTiers.SOURCE_MAX_DIM = 0 is the no-cap sentinel: the native\n  strideFor and the encoded ArgbScale.fit already pass a frame through\n  untouched at a non-positive maxDim, so no new scaling path exists.\n  Pause (Play->Pause) and the natural clip end each issue exactly ",
 "added": [],
 "removed": [],
